{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_page", "label": "The in operator", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_in_operator", "label": "in operator narrowing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When two object types differ by which properties they have and there is no discriminant or constructor, in is the only built-in narrowing left. It costs clarity: the check names a property rather than a variant, so a rename silently changes which branch runs."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_optional_properties", "label": "Optional properties break in narrowing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "in narrows on declared properties. If the distinguishing property is optional, a value of that type may lack it at runtime, so the else branch stays a union."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_prototype_chain", "label": "in walks the prototype chain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "in checks the prototype chain, so 'toString' in {} is true. Object.hasOwn is the safer runtime check for untrusted data even though it does not narrow."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_narrows_object_not_key", "label": "k in obj narrows obj never k", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A common misreading: k in obj narrows the object, never the key. Narrow the key with a type predicate returning k is keyof T."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_prefer_discriminant", "label": "Prefer a discriminant for designed types", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "in is right for shapes you do not control. For shapes you design, a discriminant is clearer, survives refactoring, and enables exhaustiveness checking."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_page", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_in_operator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_in_operator", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_optional_properties", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-2-narrowing/03-in-operator-narrowing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_in_operator", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_2_narrowing_03_in_operator_narrowing_prototype_chain"